  "notes": [
    "Venue frame: metres, x east, y north. Directions are compass bearings in degrees. Schema: docs/venue-file.md.",
    "Fictional (#36). Pairings name the version-8 conditions files (schema 6, finite pressure lanes, #303, tuned 2026-10-01); schema 2 so the geography shapes the pressure field (ADR 0008).",
    "Each pairing's geographic grid is laid square to its mean wind: 100 m cells, 500 m either side of the start line centre, from 300 m below it to 700 m above, which covers the race area at the seeded mean's full ±10° with a 360 m beat.",
    "Land lies beyond the race area at every seeded mean, at least 30 m clear of it, for the largest fleet and the longest beat: the offline venue check (VenueCheck, #83) and the sailability check (VenueSailability) pass for every pairing.",
    "Tidal estuary, the current venue (#11, #12): the one venue with a current. It runs north-east (the flood, up the estuary) to south-west (the ebb) between a salt-marsh edge on the north-west bank and a sea wall on the south-east.",
    "The channel (depth at least half the deepest, VenueCheck.channelFraction) runs down the middle of the reach, with shallows either side reaching the banks; the deepest water, 8 m, is in the race area of both pairings. Shallows turn 20 deg ahead of the channel and run slower (strength by depth to the 2/3 power, Manning). No headland eddies.",
    "Peak current 2 kn at the deepest water (the top of #11's range, #14's sailability case), a tide clock 19 times real time, and any tide state at the gun: #106 vets every state.",
    "Classic oscillating from 225, straight down the reach, so the course runs along the channel: a foul tide there is the sailability check's worst case, and still passes in a 25 % lull. A little more pressure down the open channel, lane spots along it.",
    "Gusty offshore from 315, off the marsh: the course crosses the channel. Up to 4 deg of bend and 8 % less pressure off the marsh edge, lane spots down the creek mouths.",
    "The reed-bed edge texture (docs/assets-manifest.md) is a tile for the chart (#115), not a landmark, so it isn't listed here.",
    "Geographic grids, side tendencies and the current are placeholders until the bot suite and play teach what reads well.",
    "Version 2 is version 1 with its conditions refs at version 8, the owner's lane tuning (2026-10-01). Everything else is version 1's."
  ],
